{"name":"Masala","hex":"#57534b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"masala","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many blends of spices used in Indian cuisine, most often containing cardamom, coriander, mace together with pepper, nutmeg, fennel seeds, jeera etc.","Any dish prepared with such spices."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masala"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spice mix","blocks":[{"text":"Spice mixes are blended spices or herbs. When a certain combination of herbs or spices is called for in a recipe, it is convenient to blend these ingredients beforehand. Blends such as chili powder, curry powder, herbes de Provence, garlic salt, and other seasoned salts are traditionally sold pre-made by grocers, and sometimes baking blends such as pumpkin pie spice are also available. These spice mixes are also easily made by the home cook for later use."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Garam_Masala.JPG/330px-Garam_Masala.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice_mix","wikidata":"Q1521067"},{"title":"Masala chai","blocks":[{"text":"Masala chai is a popular beverage originating from India. It is made by adding aromatic herbs and spices to chai, which is made from brewing black tea in milk and water, and sweetening with sugar, often using aeration techniques only performed by masters or \"tevanas\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Chai_In_Sakora.jpg/330px-Chai_In_Sakora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masala_chai","wikidata":"Q877661"},{"title":"Masala (2013 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Masala is a 2013 Indian Telugu-language action comedy film written and directed by K. Vijaya Bhaskar. It is produced by D. Suresh Babu and Sravanthi Ravi Kishore under the Suresh Productions and Sri Sravanthi Movies banners. The film stars Venkatesh, Ram Pothineni, Anjali and Shazahn Padamsee with music composed by S. Thaman. It is a remake of the 2012 Hindi film Bol Bachchan The film released worldwide on 14 November 2013. Upon release, the film received mixed reviews from critics with appreciation to the cast performances."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Masala_telugu_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masala_(2013_film)","wikidata":"Q16251470"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Pumpkin_Pie_Spice.jpg/500px-Pumpkin_Pie_Spice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Pumpkin_Pie_Spice.jpg/500px-Pumpkin_Pie_Spice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A container of pumpkin pie spice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APumpkin_Pie_Spice.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Khmeli_suneli.JPG/500px-Khmeli_suneli.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Khmeli_suneli.JPG/500px-Khmeli_suneli.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bowl of khmeli suneli","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKhmeli_suneli.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Gulfbaharatingredients.gif/330px-Gulfbaharatingredients.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Gulfbaharatingredients.gif/330px-Gulfbaharatingredients.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ingredients for a Gulf-style baharat","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGulf